This replaces "[PATCH v3 0/6] Add just process-email" [1] with a
standalone tool, as agreed in the reply to that series [2].

The just recipes ran from the trunk workspace, the same tree the agent
edits. When a pass moved that workspace, the loop lost its own notify
recipe and died after answering a message. lab-process-mail runs from
a copy installed with pkg under ~/local, and carries the agent's
instructions in a prompt installed beside it, so no pass can change
the loop or the procedure it runs under.

Patch 1 extracts v3 as it stood, rebase bug included: the loop, the
update before each pass, the inbox check, ntfy, and the skill text
(now prompt.md). The prompt answers one named message and does not
loop. Patch 2 packages it the way dotfiles/emacs does, with no
LOCALBASE in the package, and adds "just install" in
src/lab-process-mail.

Patch 3 fixes the rebase that cut work off a prerequisite it was built
on, with a test that fails before it. On the current repo the rebase
roots are identical before and after, so today's work moves exactly
as it did.

Patch 4 gives the agent ~/lab/work.jj, so a pass can no longer move
the working copy of ~/lab/default.jj. I chose a workspace the tool
makes over telling the agent in the prompt to make one, because the
tool can guarantee it and a test can check it; the agent stays free to
do whatever it likes inside that workspace.

Patch 5 puts ~/local/bin on the claude user's path, and patch 6
removes the process-email skill, pointing CLAUDE.md at the prompt.

To try it:

    cd src/lab-process-mail
    just test
    just install
    NOTIFY_URL=https://ntfy.sh/<topic> ~/local/bin/lab-process-mail

Notes:

- v3's "Mount a secrets directory" patch is not carried over. The tool
  reads NOTIFY_URL only, so the operator passes the topic in. If you
  still want the jail to mount a secret, it can follow separately, but
  login.conf cannot read a file into the environment, so something
  else would still have to set NOTIFY_URL from it.
- "Versioned patches must have interdiffs" [3] is still open in my
  inbox. Once this lands, the place to fix it is prompt.md, not the
  skill this series removes.
- This series is new rather than v4, since every patch is new. v3 is
  superseded and can be dropped.

